Dialogue: 1,0:00:00.08,0:00:03.96,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(490,1160)}Two testing reports in Amy\NMihaljevic’s case concerned
Dialogue: 1,0:00:04.02,0:00:07.78,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(490,1160)}different evidence. Amy was\Nten when she was abducted
Dialogue: 1,0:00:07.92,0:00:09.60,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(490,1160)}in Ohio in 1989.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:10.46,0:00:15.03,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(490,1160)}In 2024, police said retesting\Nher clothing detected male
Dialogue: 1,0:00:15.09,0:00:17.79,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(490,1160)}DNA, but too little to create a\Nprofile.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:18.67,0:00:20.35,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(490,1160)}That did not identify a\Nperson.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:21.21,0:00:24.27,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(490,1160)}Separate hairs were sent for\Ntesting in California.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:25.25,0:00:29.92,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(490,1160)}In January 2026, Cleveland 19\Nreported that Astrea
Dialogue: 1,0:00:29.96,0:00:33.54,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(490,1160)}Forensics could not obtain a\Nprofile from those hairs,
Dialogue: 1,0:00:34.14,0:00:37.14,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(490,1160)}according to Detective\NSergeant Jay Elish.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:37.16,0:00:39.04,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(490,1160)}That outcome concerned the\Nhairs.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:39.96,0:00:42.94,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(490,1160)}It did not erase the separate\Nclothing-DNA finding.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:43.88,0:00:46.16,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(490,1160)}Investigators were continuing\NDNA work;
Dialogue: 1,0:00:46.94,0:00:49.08,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(490,1160)}neither report announced an\Nidentification.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:01.60,0:00:08.60,Fact,,0,0,0,,Amy Mihaljevic • abducted in Ohio\Nin 1989 • age 10
Dialogue: 2,0:00:10.46,0:00:17.46,Fact,,0,0,0,,2024 • clothing DNA: too little for a\Nprofile
Dialogue: 2,0:00:18.67,0:00:21.21,Fact,,0,0,0,,Detection ≠ identification
Dialogue: 2,0:00:21.21,0:00:25.25,Fact,,0,0,0,,Separate evidence: hairs tested in\NCalifornia
